{
  "_doc": "One Phase 0 gear search per DPS spec of the DPS Report, for tools/rotopt/bis_phase0.sh. req is the report build the fight comes from (tools/dps_report/req), talents override its talents, start is the starting gear in equipment order (head to ranged, null for an empty slot, \"req\" for the report's item) and startEnchants keeps the report's enchant on each filled slot but the off hand. weapons is the setup (two-hand, dual-wield, one-hand or any, see applyWeaponRules in gear.go), and mhTypes and ohTypes limit the weapon types in each hand. dir is the sim UI folder the lists go in, as ui/<dir>/bis/level60_phase0_<spec>.bis.json unless out names the file. gearOut is the gear set of the list's picks with their enchants, for the sim UI and the DPS Report, as ui/<dir>/gear_sets/level60_phase0_<spec>.gear.json. A tank or healer spec (2026-11-25) has bench (tank or heal) and reqFile, its preset in tools/tankbench/req or tools/healbench/req, in place of req. A tank's tankPreset is its preset's weight (balanced, max-threat, max-survival). A healer's healRoles are the roles it's scored in, and raidReqFile is its raid role preset. scoreRef is the score on the synthetic set the gold line goes by: a tank class's Balanced preset score, a healer's damage carried in percent, the mean of its roles. bis_phase0.sh has the rest (Tanks and healers).",
